course: dictionary
lesson: 15810
title: Unchanging
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that things stay exactly the same, and unchanging is one of them. Break it into parts: un- means not, and change means to become different. So unchanging means not becoming different. «The rules of our game were unchanging: they were the same every time we played.» The rules never changed, so unchanging means staying the same.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Every morning, Mia's routine was unchanging: breakfast, school, reading, then bed.» Routine tells you the same things happen in the same order, and every morning shows it happens again and again. So unchanging means always the same.
explain: Writers use unchanging to show that something is steady and reliable, or sometimes dull. «The desert looked unchanging, mile after mile of yellow sand.» Is the desert calm and steady, or boring? The sentence leaves you to decide. Ask yourself: does the writer want me to trust this thing, or to feel bored by it?
fact: Unchanging means staying the same all the time and never changing.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unchanging means not changing.
fact: Some laws of nature and the speed of light are unchanging.
fact: Unchanging can describe something steady and reliable, or something dull.
fact: The opposite idea is changing, which means becoming different over time.
exercise: «The rules of the game were unchanging.» What does unchanging mean? | *Staying the same all the time | Changing again and again | Hidden from view | Very loud and noisy
exercise: In unchanging, what does the part un- mean? | Again | Very | Before | *Not
exercise: Which word is the closest opposite of unchanging? | Steady | Reliable | *Changing | Dull
test: «Every morning the bus follows the same unchanging route.» What does unchanging route mean here? | A route that changes every day | A route that goes underground | A route for bikes only | *A route that is always the same
test: Which sentence shows something that stays the same? | *«The bus timetable was unchanging: the bus left at eight every morning.» | «The river rose after the rain.» | «The clouds kept shifting into new shapes.» | «Our puppy grew bigger every week.»
exam: Which word would you use to describe a rule that never changes? | Changing | *Unchanging | Unhappy | Sudden
